# # Q4: How does the market value of investments fit into the balance sheet?
** IFRS 9 is treated in four categories, and the market value is reflected in a completely different way**:
- ** Holding subsidiary** (Riot/Supercell/Miniclip) <unk> Consolidated statement (no "investment" subject exists)
- ** Associated enterprises** (fasthand/post/post/general security etc.) ** The equity law subject "Investment in associated companies" (** does not reflect market value**)
- **FVTPL** (More than/Kyoto/US Group) **(Most of post-spoty/Snap) ** "Financial assets" (** Change in fair value directly into profit statement**)
- **FVOCI** (Small strategic equity) ** "Other financial assets" (fair value change OCI,** no profit statement**)

** This is why the GPS net profit fluctuations are so high and the NO-GAAP relative stability** - the classification of investments determines how market value fluctuations enter gains and losses.

